{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && sed -n '46,58p' update-stage5.json\"","aggregated_output":"          3\n        ]\n      },\n      \"conclusion\": \"holds\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The witnessed conditional execution is the defect: the automatic snapshot condition of a node that recovered through InstallSnapshot is permanently true while the node is idle, so it keeps writing fresh snapshots of unchanged state. Receipt dd59f37872d240548eff168eb821901f (completed, exit 0, tests_passed) parsed five events. Index 0 recovery_state for node server-9f900c62...: the snapshot index advanced from 62 to 202 across the reconnect while the log store last index stayed 62, with log_store_below_snapshot_index true and snapshot_advanced_over_log_store true, i.e. a real InstallSnapshot recovery whose log store was left below the installed snapshot index. Index 1 window_start for that node: should_snapshot true, snapshot index 202, last snapshot index 202, log store last index 62, applied index 202. Index 3 recovered_window_end after 22 samples of 40ms with applied_delta 0: distinct_snapshot_ids 15, snapshot_created_without_new_entries true, newest snapshot index still 202 while the newest ID moved from 2-202-1791708222798 to 2-202-1791708223751, and should_snapshot still true - comparison_index 0 holds with the victim_window admission matched to index 1. The source explains the mechanism: shouldSnapshot (snapshot.go:106-120) compares the log store's LastIndex with the last snapshot index using an unsigned subtraction with no ordering guard, while the snapshot-aware index used elsewhere is max(lastLogIndex, lastSnapshotIndex) (state.go:159-163); installSnapshot (raft.go:1814-1950) sets the last snapshot index to the installed index and compacts with min(snapIdx, lastLogIdx-trailingLogs) (snapshot.go:216-240), so a node whose log store sits below the snapshot keeps that lower index, and runSnapshots (snapshot.go:72-102) calls takeSnapshot every SnapshotInterval while the condition stays true. takeSnapshot succeeds because the FSM-reported index equals the installed snapshot index, which is not below the committed configuration index (snapshot.go:125-211). In the same receipt the control operands are recorded: index 2 and index 4 for the leader, should_snapshot false with a log store index equal to its snapshot index and distinct_snapshot_ids 1 at index 202 over the same window with applied_delta 0; that comparison's outcome in this receipt is unknown only because the shared end-event name prevented correlation, and the successor harness re-requests it with role-specific event names. Consequence and severity: on a node that recovered by snapshot and then stays idle, the node writes a full-state snapshot every SnapshotInterval indefinitely, with the snapshot store reaping older copies - repeated avoidable IO and FSM Snapshot() work rather than a safety or availability violation.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"e2a8cfd757e74ee4965e45968de09795-gap-2\": \"Yes, and nothing in the observed path raises the log store index to prevent the repeat. In receipt dd59f37872d240548eff168eb821901f (exit 0) the recovered node's log store last index stayed 62 while its snapshot index was 202 (event index 0, log_store_below_snapshot_index true), shouldSnapshot reported true at window start (index 1) and still true at window end (index 3), and over the 900ms window with applied_delta 0 the node produced 15 distinct snapshot IDs whose newest index remained 202 - so a fresh snapshot at the same index was created roughly every SnapshotInterval. The leader observed in the same window kept shouldSnapshot false with 1 distinct snapshot ID at the same index 202 (indices 2 and 4). The mechanism is the unsigned delta in snapshot.go:106-120 measured against the log store's own LastIndex rather than the snapshot-aware index, combined with installSnapshot setting the snapshot index above the surviving log store index (raft.go:1814-1950, snapshot.go:216-240) and runSnapshots sampling the condition every SnapshotInterval (snapshot.go:72-102).\",\n      },\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"e2a8cfd757e74ee4965e45968de09795-knowledge-4\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"shouldSnapshot compares the log store's own last index with the snapshot index using an unsigned subtraction with no ordering guard.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
